(a) In support and furtherance of its findings and determination that the historical, cultural and aesthetic heritage of the City of Clarkston is among its most valued and important assets and that the preservation of this heritage is essential to the promotion of the health, prosperity and general welfare of the people;
(b) In order to stimulate revitalization of the business districts and historic neighborhoods and to protect and enhance local historic and aesthetic attractions to tourists and thereby promote and stimulate business;
(c) In order to enhance the opportunities for federal or state tax benefits under relevant provisions of federal or state law; and
